[{:db/id "q-160604/selection/bdb344504abc3a20477be3b0061a467b51fce04e586ae596a6ef1bbf0033c4ee" :answer/id #uuid "ad78102c-a35a-5865-8b43-be9ccd0cb84b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160604/selection/82378bb002194b0c638448925c517772d649ad66c7e33ee485a6eb0c3c0541a4" :answer/id #uuid "92039967-027f-5da8-9938-49a2dda57598" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160604/selection/d037fb8cf08736501438259d060f65c7d8e4deabf8118415f202107f91c60ade" :answer/id #uuid "39c303c9-fbc6-5ec7-a14c-8b2e0ae13cd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160604/selection/b4ac6936776440214aaebffba73d7fd5fde48538e542fa8a6de8788032995d2c" :answer/id #uuid "1b0632fb-3d52-5da4-af02-c1819f76c81c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160604/selection/77baf6fcc8dc4d610efea7557c3e7a0eaeff3474a3041467497c38fcb9cf530e" :answer/id #uuid "838dc101-84d0-512c-8124-9438de63fd6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160604/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d57dbc25-968c-5e11-a321-b70f85864241" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160604/selection/82378bb002194b0c638448925c517772d649ad66c7e33ee485a6eb0c3c0541a4" :answer-field/choices ["q-160604/selection/bdb344504abc3a20477be3b0061a467b51fce04e586ae596a6ef1bbf0033c4ee" "q-160604/selection/82378bb002194b0c638448925c517772d649ad66c7e33ee485a6eb0c3c0541a4" "q-160604/selection/d037fb8cf08736501438259d060f65c7d8e4deabf8118415f202107f91c60ade" "q-160604/selection/b4ac6936776440214aaebffba73d7fd5fde48538e542fa8a6de8788032995d2c" "q-160604/selection/77baf6fcc8dc4d610efea7557c3e7a0eaeff3474a3041467497c38fcb9cf530e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160604" :question/id #uuid "0db007c7-21dc-5c25-8511-bf48ebe3ced5" :question/math-academy-id "q-160604" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx={v}^{2}-u,\\,y=uv.\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{3}$ under the action of $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=x(t),\\,y=t,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the function $x(t).$" :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{3}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{3},$ we have $v=1$ and $1\\ge u\\ge 0.$ Substituting $v=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =({v}^{2}-u,\\,uv) \\\\  & =({1}^{2}-u,\\,u(1)) \\\\  & =(1-u,\\,u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{3}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=1-u,\\,y=u,\\,1\\ge u\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=1-t,\\,y(t)=t,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-160604/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf2d579-5da0-5061-94f2-eec22eae7902"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160604"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-225023/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "81cc939a-0477-58a8-af0d-13f8cd4c92ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225023/selection/c990269799e88ca034500a3fd3413c3af18ea2ec1ebc05dddd4ad4a5ab508432" :answer/id #uuid "69e8cb4c-624f-5872-b7d2-857562c00302" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225023/selection/b4ac6936776440214aaebffba73d7fd5fde48538e542fa8a6de8788032995d2c" :answer/id #uuid "0983463b-547d-5b80-bc5b-d85e2b533091" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225023/selection/4153e51d0dadbc77137e2cf780b94e4ff3a779978668f53d711546d3bdd6f260" :answer/id #uuid "49c5a9b1-5a15-5b4a-8291-0ff264186db4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225023/selection/7d9187d5c22ac5d5d33ef4b4bb6b14a4a6be6da74671d1a7062e7335f1de012b" :answer/id #uuid "0631f952-a6a0-52cf-82f5-222a0a9d7d46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225023/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d58d19fa-651c-5c7b-8916-ee5490810e50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-225023/selection/7d9187d5c22ac5d5d33ef4b4bb6b14a4a6be6da74671d1a7062e7335f1de012b" :answer-field/choices ["q-225023/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-225023/selection/c990269799e88ca034500a3fd3413c3af18ea2ec1ebc05dddd4ad4a5ab508432" "q-225023/selection/b4ac6936776440214aaebffba73d7fd5fde48538e542fa8a6de8788032995d2c" "q-225023/selection/4153e51d0dadbc77137e2cf780b94e4ff3a779978668f53d711546d3bdd6f260" "q-225023/selection/7d9187d5c22ac5d5d33ef4b4bb6b14a4a6be6da74671d1a7062e7335f1de012b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-225023" :question/id #uuid "6706b3e3-ba1f-5e48-a0c6-87c0de600ccd" :question/math-academy-id "q-225023" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=v(2-u),\\,y=u{v}^{3}.\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{3}$ under the action of $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=x(t),\\,y=t,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the function $x(t).$" :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{3}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{3},$ we have $1\\ge u\\ge 0$ and $v=1.$ Substituting $v=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(v(2-u),\\,u{v}^{3}) \\\\  & =(1(2-u),\\,u(1)^{3}) \\\\  & =(2-u,u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{3}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=2-u,\\,y=u,\\,1\\ge u\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=2-t,\\,y(t)=t,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-225023/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf2d579-5da0-5061-94f2-eec22eae7902"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-225023"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-160605"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=u-v,\\,y=u(1+v).\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{4}$ under the action of $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-t,\\,y=y(t),\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the function $y(t).$" :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{4}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{4},$ we have $u=0$ and $1\\ge v\\ge 0.$ Substituting $u=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(u-v,\\,u(1+v)) \\\\  & =(0-v,\\,0(1+v)) \\\\  & =(-v,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{4}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=-v,\\,y=0,\\,1\\ge v\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=-t,\\,y(t)=0,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-160602/selection/b77633b0368d8725fb5dcaece4aed8339ab5d3308acf6e8e6f2f935193fda378" :answer/id #uuid "44e0b0ea-df09-53a7-ba35-781dd3517ec0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160602/selection/77baf6fcc8dc4d610efea7557c3e7a0eaeff3474a3041467497c38fcb9cf530e" :answer/id #uuid "9e15fcce-133b-5866-bfe8-a0cd0a203451" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160602/selection/d037fb8cf08736501438259d060f65c7d8e4deabf8118415f202107f91c60ade" :answer/id #uuid "f708db4b-5a18-5fe2-addb-cf8a5e76dcf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160602/selection/c5ad98556b70934f51782e5a9a0d433f934e12cf217e6d147924438567564dc2" :answer/id #uuid "982de388-e92d-57b2-b926-ccea83bd34d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160602/selection/cb9ad14c4d0189695cf5d02baf58f5eec7ac941edc170f6dffed142cbab880f5" :answer/id #uuid "75a71bf9-59b2-510c-ab1b-3dbe35a7f415" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160602/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "50321977-6aa3-53cb-b955-adf7d331a54a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160602/selection/cb9ad14c4d0189695cf5d02baf58f5eec7ac941edc170f6dffed142cbab880f5" :answer-field/choices ["q-160602/selection/b77633b0368d8725fb5dcaece4aed8339ab5d3308acf6e8e6f2f935193fda378" "q-160602/selection/77baf6fcc8dc4d610efea7557c3e7a0eaeff3474a3041467497c38fcb9cf530e" "q-160602/selection/d037fb8cf08736501438259d060f65c7d8e4deabf8118415f202107f91c60ade" "q-160602/selection/c5ad98556b70934f51782e5a9a0d433f934e12cf217e6d147924438567564dc2" "q-160602/selection/cb9ad14c4d0189695cf5d02baf58f5eec7ac941edc170f6dffed142cbab880f5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160602" :question/id #uuid "161ff342-2f4e-5550-9a79-f32353673b94" :question/math-academy-id "q-160602" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx={u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,y=u.\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{1}$ under the action of $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=x(t),\\,y=t,\\,0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$\n\nFind the function $x(t).$" :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{1}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{1},$ we have $v=0$ and $0\\le u\\le 1.$ Substituting $v=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =({u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,u) \\\\  & =({u}^{2}-{0}^{2},\\,u) \\\\  & =({u}^{2},\\,u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{1}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx={u}^{2},\\,y=u,\\,0\\le u\\le 1.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2},\\,y(t)=t,\\,0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-160602/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf2d579-5da0-5061-94f2-eec22eae7902"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160602"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-225021/selection/4153e51d0dadbc77137e2cf780b94e4ff3a779978668f53d711546d3bdd6f260" :answer/id #uuid "42cb55f4-1037-5780-89d4-31f02e61d891" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225021/selection/d037fb8cf08736501438259d060f65c7d8e4deabf8118415f202107f91c60ade" :answer/id #uuid "7b82aed9-6f50-5851-81a7-66bfae53ae6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225021/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "a22c3f4e-58dc-5a04-992a-80895a0f95cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225021/selection/eaba4da4447c9b33a895d609a3f81feab98b794b9799550831cc4a744e96cb0d" :answer/id #uuid "b1be0fa4-7e38-55a0-90d3-10e91f53fe31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225021/selection/b4ac6936776440214aaebffba73d7fd5fde48538e542fa8a6de8788032995d2c" :answer/id #uuid "6a9e2ff9-1c23-5f96-9893-cf3a7fb5d599" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225021/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ab5ea10e-326c-58c0-8dd7-46e42d67753a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-225021/selection/eaba4da4447c9b33a895d609a3f81feab98b794b9799550831cc4a744e96cb0d" :answer-field/choices ["q-225021/selection/4153e51d0dadbc77137e2cf780b94e4ff3a779978668f53d711546d3bdd6f260" "q-225021/selection/d037fb8cf08736501438259d060f65c7d8e4deabf8118415f202107f91c60ade" "q-225021/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-225021/selection/eaba4da4447c9b33a895d609a3f81feab98b794b9799550831cc4a744e96cb0d" "q-225021/selection/b4ac6936776440214aaebffba73d7fd5fde48538e542fa8a6de8788032995d2c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-225021" :question/id #uuid "9c159cd1-4182-5756-b6e5-bbda60897fa5" :question/math-academy-id "q-225021" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=v-u,\\,y=u(u+v).\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{2}$ under the action of $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=x(t),\\,y=1+t,\\,0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$\n\nFind the function $x(t).$" :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{2}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{2},$ we have $u=1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$ Substituting $u=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(v-u,\\,u(u+v)) \\\\  & =(v-1,\\,1(1+v)) \\\\  & =(v-1,1+v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{2}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=v-1,\\,y=1+v,\\,0\\le v\\le 1.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=t-1,\\,y(t)=1+t,\\,0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-225021/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf2d579-5da0-5061-94f2-eec22eae7902"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-225021"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-225046/selection/a0d5fd23c3612246bb88aa1e0d30b4c34bb150a18fe1830ef08961b7eba44aab" :answer/id #uuid "ff581eec-c1b6-56ff-a408-d95193799f92" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,-1)$ and $(-1,-1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225046/selection/201339cbf9416f70a6efb1434df0bd60b126867dd3d91c46b7bb4c730a7156a4" :answer/id #uuid "d6d78246-2d8b-539b-8e8d-6954ab089777" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,-1)$ and $(0,-1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225046/selection/82ddb883cb035aa1dbdf0e7848a235ec444c881a6975bbc3e405d6319b1f3a50" :answer/id #uuid "2268468d-2962-5a00-8dce-4608dea81a92" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,0)$ and $(-1,-1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225046/selection/8684b95d675d9e4aa4a2762effbeb96b5acd248efb484822a1fa416d5558429b" :answer/id #uuid "8699d9e4-2f92-51b8-ac6d-ad58f446c597" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,-1)$ and $(-1,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225046/selection/5fe4ca80279b454ade2c71bea882795b1b1cb60813a62ee55c37fa95ad2b44ed" :answer/id #uuid "3cd34303-960d-5ce9-9aac-f7cd6bc46932" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,-1)$ and $(1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225046/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "685fce89-66f4-580b-91f9-8f37b19a6445" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-225046/selection/201339cbf9416f70a6efb1434df0bd60b126867dd3d91c46b7bb4c730a7156a4" :answer-field/choices ["q-225046/selection/a0d5fd23c3612246bb88aa1e0d30b4c34bb150a18fe1830ef08961b7eba44aab" "q-225046/selection/201339cbf9416f70a6efb1434df0bd60b126867dd3d91c46b7bb4c730a7156a4" "q-225046/selection/82ddb883cb035aa1dbdf0e7848a235ec444c881a6975bbc3e405d6319b1f3a50" "q-225046/selection/8684b95d675d9e4aa4a2762effbeb96b5acd248efb484822a1fa416d5558429b" "q-225046/selection/5fe4ca80279b454ade2c71bea882795b1b1cb60813a62ee55c37fa95ad2b44ed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-225046" :question/id #uuid "7653f22c-a2c4-5d20-9a2b-cda9efc3f200" :question/math-academy-id "q-225046" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ and its **directed** boundary $∂Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, where $Δ$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=(u-1)v,\\,y=uv-1.\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{4}$ under the action of $T$ is a **directed** line segment. Find the endpoints of this segment, stated in the order that they are traversed." :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{4}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{4},$ we have $u=0$ and $1\\ge v\\ge 0.$ Substituting $u=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =((u-1)v,\\,uv-1) \\\\  & =((0-1)v,\\,(0)v-1) \\\\  & =(-v,-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{4}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=-v,\\,y=-1,\\,1\\ge v\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=-t,\\,y(t)=-1,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThis is a horizontal line segment with endpoints $(-1,-1)$ and $(0,-1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/48ae89e14005e5fc21f0693e769e6214c1c9a94ba0cd63e7ce08d9771fbf82f1.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-225046/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d96918f5-2a27-5413-8fcd-a6c8060a9342"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-225046"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-225036/selection/565a5672d7a54f758531d3a18df05ba6f5360e85e49636c07cae4b021d14c7f9" :answer/id #uuid "e2677b7d-62f2-5087-8272-1558dee9d7c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0)$ and $(1,2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225036/selection/a694c5ba917545b46ee6a8505ae8d62e40fcee4c5922de11f59da72b9e79991d" :answer/id #uuid "e3c8dcb8-ca06-5119-b673-8a8c933b6d4d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,1)$ and $(2,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225036/selection/8b067a2dc91df75541e08b39f9c74af38562584b9f356f884d56865f84bb649c" :answer/id #uuid "0d02b29a-1fed-5b89-ab1a-25b517fecb46" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,2)$ and $(1,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225036/selection/81f6d637bab482920904b8b032354abd2fceb8ea23de5dcc56c412532feb6d2b" :answer/id #uuid "8ef6252d-5685-5df9-b855-ee941df0d10e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,2)$ and $(0,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225036/selection/dab3e9b86dd8e475528a44dbca4b54be3c18e37ee371b5ab12f05f80e5764571" :answer/id #uuid "37e81f62-50d2-5f75-a5b1-3f4bb33c121d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,2)$ and $(1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225036/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9744e5b6-62ce-5bdf-8668-11e351fa5cba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-225036/selection/565a5672d7a54f758531d3a18df05ba6f5360e85e49636c07cae4b021d14c7f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-225036/selection/565a5672d7a54f758531d3a18df05ba6f5360e85e49636c07cae4b021d14c7f9" "q-225036/selection/a694c5ba917545b46ee6a8505ae8d62e40fcee4c5922de11f59da72b9e79991d" "q-225036/selection/8b067a2dc91df75541e08b39f9c74af38562584b9f356f884d56865f84bb649c" "q-225036/selection/81f6d637bab482920904b8b032354abd2fceb8ea23de5dcc56c412532feb6d2b" "q-225036/selection/dab3e9b86dd8e475528a44dbca4b54be3c18e37ee371b5ab12f05f80e5764571"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-225036" :question/id #uuid "7a79d324-570b-5caa-a973-18fefab2c0a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-225036" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ and its **directed** boundary $∂Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, where $Δ$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=u-{v}^{2},\\,y=2(u-v).\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{1}$ under the action of $T$ is a **directed** line segment. Find the endpoints of this segment, stated in the order that they are traversed." :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{1}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{1},$ we have $v=0$ and $0\\le u\\le 1.$ Substituting $v=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(u-{v}^{2},\\,2(u-v)) \\\\  & =(u-{0}^{2},\\,2(u-0)) \\\\  & =(u,2u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{1}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y=2u,\\,0\\le u\\le 1.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=t,\\,y(t)=2t,\\,0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$\n\nThis is a line segment with endpoints $(0,0)$ and $(1,2)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/9d9c8e967d4290f0a75e071762ff05c97b12367f43f8a1a965fff09efa64743b.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-225036/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d96918f5-2a27-5413-8fcd-a6c8060a9342"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-225036"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-225119/selection/5489f58ee249d158da660112d69e42241de18bb061be449f328c9e00a67bae9d" :answer/id #uuid "6d754227-7d35-5ec4-a660-65b57c94f2d7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,-2)$ and $(1,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225119/selection/90e36893e6199c7bb6210fdf8b96b5053c32d7c8f68eeacb38c7813063b75f1b" :answer/id #uuid "e28e5313-2744-5a0f-86d4-f2cd09643bbc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0)$ and $(1,-2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225119/selection/473d12886769d8323300ff934b3da67ccb777d1a44d87858a99eac4a34e5ca47" :answer/id #uuid "398b8556-b350-5de4-b550-d63d5e4d64e7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-2)$ and $(0,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225119/selection/d35e7bc58758424374aabc0bd4a25b5a636275aabea87ebe2bf843098c6abd95" :answer/id #uuid "9eba46dc-f1bb-5cf8-a928-0bc5fdd2f9d6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,0)$ and $(0,-2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225119/selection/51e5a152b0815d4bde62ac73f30310046655b563bc6e54bd8201687d2dcc2782" :answer/id #uuid "5905a13c-973b-5cd5-be20-dca6619b2dfd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,1)$ and $(-2,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225119/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d704e77-71f5-5eb7-a8ff-12f754b2fc83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-225119/selection/90e36893e6199c7bb6210fdf8b96b5053c32d7c8f68eeacb38c7813063b75f1b" :answer-field/choices ["q-225119/selection/5489f58ee249d158da660112d69e42241de18bb061be449f328c9e00a67bae9d" "q-225119/selection/90e36893e6199c7bb6210fdf8b96b5053c32d7c8f68eeacb38c7813063b75f1b" "q-225119/selection/473d12886769d8323300ff934b3da67ccb777d1a44d87858a99eac4a34e5ca47" "q-225119/selection/d35e7bc58758424374aabc0bd4a25b5a636275aabea87ebe2bf843098c6abd95" "q-225119/selection/51e5a152b0815d4bde62ac73f30310046655b563bc6e54bd8201687d2dcc2782"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-225119" :question/id #uuid "00015daa-fef5-50ba-aa66-6c05adbe786b" :question/math-academy-id "q-225119" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ and its **directed** boundary $∂Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, where $Δ$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=u+4v,\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}(v-4u).\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{1}$ under the action of $T$ is a **directed** line segment. Find the endpoints of this segment, stated in the order that they are traversed." :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{1}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{1},$ we have $v=0$ and $0\\le u\\le 1.$ Substituting $v=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(u+4v,\\,\\frac{1}{2}(v-4u)) \\\\  & =(u+4(0),\\,\\frac{1}{2}(0-4u)) \\\\  & =(u,-2u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{1}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y=-2u,\\,0\\le u\\le 1.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=t,\\,y(t)=-2t,\\,0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$\n\nThis is a line segment with endpoints $(0,0)$ and $(1,-2)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/9af81ffe277395ce00ef597235bb8f440ff22e5da9db5cbe3266dae8ba0fe281.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-225119/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d96918f5-2a27-5413-8fcd-a6c8060a9342"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-225119"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-225042/selection/e27a9b613e5d6436dceae677172f744b8c91f6a98e34730af5aa8c15426d5539" :answer/id #uuid "2cc8a842-cabd-51df-86e7-e51d52bc2035" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,3)$ and $(1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225042/selection/c6b726d5fa7cd46c1cfa3057431b431a4111155b0898ed19c5f2702d9e5951b5" :answer/id #uuid "3ecd92f3-cfe0-5b04-a42f-b82e3d8e835b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,0)$ and $(1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225042/selection/9207f198b39ff68f75c4065e14b9ac0708b6e97a57da9550e253aa72b4cb71fe" :answer/id #uuid "234e7884-97d1-5af9-9d66-c0613656d74e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,1)$ and $(3,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225042/selection/4218e1058a33de5baa3868b68bb3fda678dab6053d1edf27a067cdd6b11254e7" :answer/id #uuid "3d587aeb-3cb4-5577-bf20-f665d43a5152" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,1)$ and $(3,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225042/selection/93743c53682f2ef9ed6c554f75a0cb1c0472bbb24b7a3e90e0ed520f9f97dc25" :answer/id #uuid "e70242c6-8303-5da4-9eb1-ce17627f9fc6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,1)$ and $(0,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225042/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a06ba23-8d81-5120-b1bc-02387898a59b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-225042/selection/c6b726d5fa7cd46c1cfa3057431b431a4111155b0898ed19c5f2702d9e5951b5" :answer-field/choices ["q-225042/selection/e27a9b613e5d6436dceae677172f744b8c91f6a98e34730af5aa8c15426d5539" "q-225042/selection/c6b726d5fa7cd46c1cfa3057431b431a4111155b0898ed19c5f2702d9e5951b5" "q-225042/selection/9207f198b39ff68f75c4065e14b9ac0708b6e97a57da9550e253aa72b4cb71fe" "q-225042/selection/4218e1058a33de5baa3868b68bb3fda678dab6053d1edf27a067cdd6b11254e7" "q-225042/selection/93743c53682f2ef9ed6c554f75a0cb1c0472bbb24b7a3e90e0ed520f9f97dc25"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-225042" :question/id #uuid "324cbe9b-d00d-58c1-aa7d-d1e71d18ccbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-225042" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ and its **directed** boundary $∂Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, where $Δ$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx={v}^{2}+2u,\\,y=v-u.\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{3}$ under the action of $T$ is a **directed** line segment. Find the endpoints of this segment, stated in the order that they are traversed." :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{3}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{3},$ we have $v=1$ and $1\\ge u\\ge 0.$ Substituting $v=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =({v}^{2}+2u,\\,v-u) \\\\  & =({1}^{2}+2u,\\,1-u) \\\\  & =(1+2u,\\,1-u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{3}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=1+2u,\\,y=1-u,\\,1\\ge u\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=1+2t,\\,y(t)=1-t,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThis is a line segment with endpoints $(3,0)$ and $(1,1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/f75f8beceedef7d64d12c7cf1d4bc838039ecdeae3de752c45e76975f116fcb2.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-225042/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d96918f5-2a27-5413-8fcd-a6c8060a9342"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-225042"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-225122/selection/3ef944821404171782727249362983d40d7d2fec2288856a8788254bacf4e011" :answer/id #uuid "247a55cb-a972-5f19-87dc-5ac57fd8bdbf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0)$ and $(2,-1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225122/selection/6382033738073a6cdc35f35690eacedc625aefcf72a83adcd7388af73ef6541e" :answer/id #uuid "966a4c7a-5f33-5188-b102-352a87277c1f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,0)$ and $(0,-1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225122/selection/781047471c03aa07b4788dbb47d895e918d9e84b33dd3e7f5f526acfe9fa5f9d" :answer/id #uuid "ddf694b3-9d93-5b8c-a955-a3190e268ec1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,2)$ and $(0,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225122/selection/0cffb338ae96b2a2a485dba3d39d6b855072f76a07edbb16b56eb56224328d7c" :answer/id #uuid "c87e9a86-e3cc-581e-a7cb-1e56e37a211e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,-1)$ and $(2,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225122/selection/f1aeb95675d4075a94f96c224cdd3938d626d71701383dfbe14cded6e09dead8" :answer/id #uuid "ef94b90c-6acc-591d-b134-acbe2a44420d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,-1)$ and $(0,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225122/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "014cd7da-4f27-541b-ac92-d4e7957d7b65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-225122/selection/3ef944821404171782727249362983d40d7d2fec2288856a8788254bacf4e011" :answer-field/choices ["q-225122/selection/3ef944821404171782727249362983d40d7d2fec2288856a8788254bacf4e011" "q-225122/selection/6382033738073a6cdc35f35690eacedc625aefcf72a83adcd7388af73ef6541e" "q-225122/selection/781047471c03aa07b4788dbb47d895e918d9e84b33dd3e7f5f526acfe9fa5f9d" "q-225122/selection/0cffb338ae96b2a2a485dba3d39d6b855072f76a07edbb16b56eb56224328d7c" "q-225122/selection/f1aeb95675d4075a94f96c224cdd3938d626d71701383dfbe14cded6e09dead8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-225122" :question/id #uuid "1b2021c7-be96-5682-96e0-0128a770e021" :question/math-academy-id "q-225122" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ and its **directed** boundary $∂Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, where $Δ$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{3}(v+6u),\\,y=\\frac{{v}^{3}-2u}{v+2}.\n$$\n\nThe image of the side ${S}_{1}$ under the action of $T$ is a **directed** line segment. Find the endpoints of this segment, stated in the order that they are traversed." :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{1}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{1},$ we have $v=0$ and $0\\le u\\le 1.$ Substituting $v=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}(v+6u),\\,\\frac{{v}^{3}-2u}{v+2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}(0+6u),\\,\\frac{{0}^{3}-2u}{0+2}) \\\\  & =(2u,-u).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{1}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=2u,\\,y=-u,\\,0\\le u\\le 1.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=2t,\\,y(t)=-t,\\,0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$\n\nThis is a line segment with endpoints $(0,0)$ and $(2,-1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/f068883d1318acdafba39c74bc1279f6cafe803437a9b79249999df461bac8ee.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-225122/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d96918f5-2a27-5413-8fcd-a6c8060a9342"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-225122"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-225228/selection/da2010101c21f7c358617f18c2920dc216e15d09386eed16dbe16221208e3334" :answer/id #uuid "11f41c8f-22af-51a2-9a7e-f02b73afe975" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An arc of a right-opening parabola, traversed from $(0,1)$ to $(-1,2).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225228/selection/09a0c12e1efc1b299c55cfb02681835d3c48e267c075c7a9640a4d2255738e44" :answer/id #uuid "ed6b9e46-407c-5c3b-b606-f838aa42e930" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An arc of a right-opening parabola, traversed from   $(1,1)$ to $(0,2).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225228/selection/fa8bcc391ec0e88af191d0a79c2c362a983200e83953a7ccdc4cd7108c916e68" :answer/id #uuid "08dacdc8-24ed-5263-b06b-880398e1a083" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An arc of an upward-opening parabola, traversed from $(-1,2)$ to $(0,1).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225228/selection/28fa22f0a287f3f30eb9b8144f3f2389636b74b02b37d44417567ab0e17c6d52" :answer/id #uuid "8bb81e2f-2d7f-5cac-a682-5a1162c8bb8f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An arc of a upward-opening parabola, traversed from $(0,2)$ to $(1,1).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225228/selection/7dac7714c44765459069c364f7f60b761e92ec5f4190d05dcb126cdbc9a603f5" :answer/id #uuid "5a1acaad-ab31-526e-8544-d7e535f4587f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An arc of an upward-opening parabola, traversed from $(0,1)$ to $(-1,2).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225228/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "afaec246-f8ec-514a-9e97-2ad1202fef5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-225228/selection/7dac7714c44765459069c364f7f60b761e92ec5f4190d05dcb126cdbc9a603f5" :answer-field/choices ["q-225228/selection/da2010101c21f7c358617f18c2920dc216e15d09386eed16dbe16221208e3334" "q-225228/selection/09a0c12e1efc1b299c55cfb02681835d3c48e267c075c7a9640a4d2255738e44" "q-225228/selection/fa8bcc391ec0e88af191d0a79c2c362a983200e83953a7ccdc4cd7108c916e68" "q-225228/selection/28fa22f0a287f3f30eb9b8144f3f2389636b74b02b37d44417567ab0e17c6d52" "q-225228/selection/7dac7714c44765459069c364f7f60b761e92ec5f4190d05dcb126cdbc9a603f5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-225228" :question/id #uuid "5bd99021-9f7b-5102-9e9a-342e79f39167" :question/math-academy-id "q-225228" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{v-1}{u+1},\\,y=(u+v-1)^{2}+1.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the side ${S}_{4}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{4}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{4},$ we have $u=0$ and $1\\ge v\\ge 0.$ Substituting $u=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(\\frac{v-1}{u+1},\\,(u+v-1)^{2}+1) \\\\  & =(\\frac{v-1}{0+1},\\,(0+v-1)^{2}+1) \\\\  & =(v-1,\\,(v-1)^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{4}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=v-1,\\,y=(v-1)^{2}+1,\\,1\\ge v\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx=t-1,\\,y=(t-1)^{2}+1,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThese are parametric equations of a parabolic arc. Notice that if we eliminate $t$ from the equations, we get\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}+1\n$$\n\nwhich is an upward-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,1).$\n\nMoreover, the endpoints of ${S}_{4}$ are mapped to the $xy$-plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T:(0,1)\\to (\\frac{1-1}{0+1},(0+1-1)^{2}+1)=(0,1) \\\\  & T:(0,0)\\to (\\frac{0-1}{0+1},(0+0-1)^{2}+1)=(-1,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${S}_{4}$ is an arc of a upward-opening parabola, traversed from $(0,1)$ to $(-1,2).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/69a2a8ab136360c01d1a17a58dc2fc4864ae2089330a551df913b200d923f087.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-225228/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "148c9c1d-236d-571f-89be-d1c03f7c39aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-225228"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-225160/selection/5e67f25565704d189dfc916ee07c9db3a4c3d75307f1ce5c6664b35afb5d6377" :answer/id #uuid "cd7c5f50-8da3-5a7b-9df8-64e6a014f93a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An arc of a downward-opening parabola, traversed from $(1,0)$ to $(0,1).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225160/selection/161922f68308e0c63cedcdc8d1846e87ccaeca6dbf34188ac96d509dbb162435" :answer/id #uuid "10ad3d7b-ff4c-51c5-b366-20f80d306319" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An arc of a left-opening parabola, traversed from $(1,0)$ to $(0,1).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225160/selection/0c4e707898be1608ff228adcfd37db4155091bd6a132a34baacfd67124c5deef" :answer/id #uuid "bc802fa5-f4a9-51f1-89aa-9a57fdbe5c86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An arc of a downward-opening parabola, traversed from $(1,1)$ to $(2,1).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225160/selection/9fb53a5bb5aef696f849642ab7948ddcf6aad2c90fcafd128a207f84ab01c987" :answer/id #uuid "79826f9d-7b98-5f4e-9b1b-d801f341f883" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An arc of a left-opening parabola, traversed from $(0,1)$ to $(1,0).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225160/selection/2a79d712a3d5fe20048a974a69779105ccb80460b0b3371730445f384674b0ed" :answer/id #uuid "ee555fab-b466-5906-887b-2b5eb01d90fa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An arc of a downward-opening parabola, traversed from $(2,1)$ to $(1,1).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225160/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f076906e-fb75-57ee-87b3-1ee3c2ff79a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-225160/selection/161922f68308e0c63cedcdc8d1846e87ccaeca6dbf34188ac96d509dbb162435" :answer-field/choices ["q-225160/selection/5e67f25565704d189dfc916ee07c9db3a4c3d75307f1ce5c6664b35afb5d6377" "q-225160/selection/161922f68308e0c63cedcdc8d1846e87ccaeca6dbf34188ac96d509dbb162435" "q-225160/selection/0c4e707898be1608ff228adcfd37db4155091bd6a132a34baacfd67124c5deef" "q-225160/selection/9fb53a5bb5aef696f849642ab7948ddcf6aad2c90fcafd128a207f84ab01c987" "q-225160/selection/2a79d712a3d5fe20048a974a69779105ccb80460b0b3371730445f384674b0ed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-225160" :question/id #uuid "e9645ee3-f058-5cab-ba3f-d7bc67c13923" :question/math-academy-id "q-225160" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx={u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,y=1-u+v.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the side ${S}_{2}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{2}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{2},$ we have $u=1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$ Substituting $u=1$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =({u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,1-u+v) \\\\  & =({1}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,1-1+v) \\\\  & =(1-{v}^{2},\\,v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{2}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=1-{v}^{2},\\,y=v,\\,0\\le v\\le 1.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx=1-{t}^{2},\\,y=t,\\,0\\le t\\le 1.\n$$\n\nThese are parametric equations of a parabolic arc. Notice that if we eliminate $t$ from the equations, we get\n\n$$\nx=1-{y}^{2}\\,⇒\\,{y}^{2}=1-x\n$$\n\nwhich is a left-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(1,0).$\n\nMoreover, the endpoints of ${S}_{2}$ are mapped to the $xy$-plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T:(1,0)\\to ({1}^{2}-{0}^{2},1-1+0)=(1,0) \\\\  & T:(1,1)\\to ({1}^{2}-{1}^{0},1-1+1)=(0,1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${S}_{2}$ is an arc of a left-opening parabola, traversed from $(1,0)$ to $(0,1).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/995b106a25173b4e3667fd3fce04f499d7d4a549ae76414328f6e3c406ddd3c6.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-225160/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "148c9c1d-236d-571f-89be-d1c03f7c39aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-225160"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-225166/selection/6c2d816dacf5e6ed6d9696933de1910414588fc5ee725fae213c20bcaa6a79f0" :answer/id #uuid "a364c536-e3bf-5cff-9a6b-3b41724575a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An arc of a downward-opening parabola, traversed from $(0,1)$ to $(0,0).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225166/selection/d1758b180a2e99a73a783bd7428b49f13b42a257747f3bd78399608c1237c082" :answer/id #uuid "1a9b311c-1e2f-57fe-a185-d932239ca5af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An arc of a left-opening parabola, traversed from $(0,0)$ to $(0,1).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225166/selection/60de84797cc4ee7c1d263c42a9bce58467ef3235c0d89fb09c3fa383fe4e945f" :answer/id #uuid "8e4e29da-b3af-5ba4-b643-f5a1b0783856" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An arc of a left-opening parabola, traversed from $(1,0)$ to $(1,1).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225166/selection/9aaacaf2786e0b76c262d72e48685edb2c29617c8a1a5678a14f1a36357322c6" :answer/id #uuid "7507ceff-0cd1-59ae-8340-31948823029f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An arc of a left-opening parabola, traversed from $(0,1)$ to $(0,0).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225166/selection/5e67f25565704d189dfc916ee07c9db3a4c3d75307f1ce5c6664b35afb5d6377" :answer/id #uuid "9ff6126d-4212-574c-ade5-350629d1e3d6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An arc of a downward-opening parabola, traversed from $(1,0)$ to $(0,1).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225166/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d5557a50-c460-5cdb-897b-48b80492ca3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-225166/selection/d1758b180a2e99a73a783bd7428b49f13b42a257747f3bd78399608c1237c082" :answer-field/choices ["q-225166/selection/6c2d816dacf5e6ed6d9696933de1910414588fc5ee725fae213c20bcaa6a79f0" "q-225166/selection/d1758b180a2e99a73a783bd7428b49f13b42a257747f3bd78399608c1237c082" "q-225166/selection/60de84797cc4ee7c1d263c42a9bce58467ef3235c0d89fb09c3fa383fe4e945f" "q-225166/selection/9aaacaf2786e0b76c262d72e48685edb2c29617c8a1a5678a14f1a36357322c6" "q-225166/selection/5e67f25565704d189dfc916ee07c9db3a4c3d75307f1ce5c6664b35afb5d6377"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-225166" :question/id #uuid "eb748daa-00e4-5417-b9e3-8e79e21eb586" :question/math-academy-id "q-225166" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/33e48fa5bdbb034bcf489e038ccf80fc5f67baabeccacc1b7abd741183ebf05d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nx=2v(1-u-v),\\,y=\\frac{1-v}{1+u}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the side ${S}_{4}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{4}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{4},$ we have $u=0$ and $1\\ge v\\ge 0.$ Substituting $u=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(2v(1-u-v),\\,\\frac{1-v}{1+u}) \\\\  & =(2v(1-0-v),\\,\\frac{1-v}{1+0}) \\\\  & =(2v(1-v),\\,1-v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{4}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=2v(1-v),\\,y=1-v,\\,1\\ge v\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx=2t(1-t),\\,y=1-t,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThese are parametric equations of a parabolic arc. Notice that if we eliminate $t$ from the equations, we get\n\n$$\nx=2(1-y)(y)\\,⇒\\,x=-2{(y-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nwhich is a left-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\nMoreover, the endpoints of ${S}_{4}$ are mapped to the $xy$-plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T:(0,1)\\to (2(1)(1-0-1),\\frac{1-1}{1+0})=(0,0) \\\\  & T:(0,0)\\to (2(0)(1-0-0),\\frac{1-0}{1+0})=(0,1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${S}_{4}$ is an arc of a left-opening parabola, traversed from $(0,0)$ to $(0,1).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/ff3c1028da35afad6c215e88863665b5bd6647d2507af2344f9f6710f0ad6373.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-225166/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "148c9c1d-236d-571f-89be-d1c03f7c39aa"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-225166"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-225167/selection/c204cf4ef411a76294788daf2bb25a72ec8b9954a06bb52e9daefac1c4328893" :answer/id #uuid "9bb99c56-a255-5fee-b694-f2aba9d9fac6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An arc of an upward-opening parabola, traversed from $(0,0)$ to $(1,1).$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-225167/selection/89d062808b648a7f7c5